<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Trump gives Xi rare airport welcome as Chinese leader begins US state visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54e6644cf644038b41477b597c7fe628519fc15f24c92e7407e853ea86e0917a</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T01:48:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-trump-gives-xi-rare-airport-welcome-as-chinese-leader-begins-us-state-visit" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump personally welcomed Chinese President Xi Jinping at a military airfield outside Washington on Wednesday, kicking off a lavish state visit focused on trade, artificial intelligence and Iran, as the two powers seek to preserve a fragile diplomatic and economic truce.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey to hand over military base in northern Iraq to Baghdad</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f9601fb1a8eefddb6c86da3674446297380e6d6de05552ae474ebdb4c2791a6</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-24T00:02:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260924-turkey-to-hand-over-military-base-in-northern-iraq-to-baghdad" /><summary type="html">Turkey will gradually hand over control of its Bashiqa military base in northern Iraq to Baghdad, Ankara and Baghdad said Wednesday, in a move aimed at strengthening Iraqi state authority and easing a long-running source of tension between the neighbours.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>OpenAI AI agent breached Australian government website, PM says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:445dd8fa426a0b5ee760d28da6ba4ae8f9725d8eccf322d15182abfa0ef3eb9d</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T22:10:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/australia/20260923-openai-ai-agent-breached-australian-government-website-pm-says" /><summary type="html">An AI agent developed by OpenAI gained unauthorised access to an Australian government website in June, accessing public and non-public files in what Prime Minister Anthony Albanese described as the first known case of an AI agent hacking a government system.</summary><category term="Australia" /></entry><entry><title>AI leaders urge caution at UN, with Anthropic chief pledging to slow down</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f409ec29252a139afc1cb6be3521c0e8a5708fae4f47325c68cf459c99cee27d</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T21:46:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-ai-leaders-urge-caution-at-un-with-anthropic-chief-pledging-to-slow-down" /><summary type="html">Leaders of some of the world's biggest AI companies urged caution at the United Nations on Wednesday, warning that increasingly autonomous systems could outpace human oversight. Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei pledged to slow development to ensure new AI systems are safe, while OpenAI chief Sam Altman called for 'extreme care'.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Fact-checking Trump’s speech at the United Nations General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:520fbeac7a1b95e3face7d2ae2e5d4493817f9628a630211cebef65952695d7a</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T20:54:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/fact-checking-trump-s-speech-at-the-united-nations-general-assembly-1" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump’s UN address was packed with claims that are misleading, false or exaggerated. He said the US has more munitions than it could ever use, despite reports of depleting stocks. He claimed the US and Venezuela hold 60% of the world’s oil, despite the numbers not adding up, and he said he had ended the war in Gaza despite ongoing Israeli strikes and deaths since last year's ceasefire. Vedika Bahl fact-checks the speech in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Trump sparks debate over diesel export ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:59562f3ab4485c340025b09780fef96161265ec650db5cc5b17382dbf50618fa</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T20:38:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-sparks-debate-over-diesel-export-ban" /><summary type="html">The Trump administration's suggestion that it could ban or limit diesel exports has sparked furious backlash from the American oil industry. Politicians are trying to bring down soaring energy prices ahead of the midterm election in November, but critics say a ban would cause supply problems and higher prices both at home and abroad. Also in this edition - the OECD says the global economy is withstanding the energy shock better than expected, partly thanks to AI investment.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Tigray rebels seize airports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b25647b34c0e11202a6d317f285bef486cbda0343a2cdc9025a54229a8c32307</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T20:27:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tigray-rebels-seize-airports" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, concerns about South Africa's high rates of crimes are brought even more into focus this week as 11 are killed in a mass killing at a party. Also, TPLF fighters take over the airport in Tigray amidst escalating conflict with federal troops. And in eastern DR Congo, residents of Bukavu are once again searching through the ruins of their homes after another deadly fire.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>REPLAY: Ukrainian President Zelensky addresses the UN General Assembly</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dec448593e24107d81c8d943bf8b0dd072624b0de97c9443506b2c52318e131d</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T19:44:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-replay-ukrainian-president-zelensky-addresses-the-un-general-assembly" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky urged the world’s leaders Wednesday to keep choking Russia’s revenues and impede its war efforts, telling the UN General Assembly that “Russia’s revenues must remain a target”. Watch his full speech above.</summary></entry><entry><title>No, this video doesn't disprove the 9/11 attack on the south tower of the World Trade Center</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af91b93732d3ef6c9acae50ef1f7d1ece25c336680f656b0ff5baa46c8a63440</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T19:01:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-video-no-proof-plane-hit-twin-tower-9-11--3315503e2a84.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-video-no-proof-plane-hit-twin-tower-9-11" /><summary type="html">A former British member of parliament implied that a video filmed from a helicopter on September 11, 2001 shows that no planes actually hit the World Trade Center's south tower, but this claim would be unfounded. The plane that hit the south tower hit the other side of the building, which isn’t visible in the video.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Zelensky accuses Putin of using nationals of 47 countries to fight Ukraine war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9380552302f4bc700c90e2421a46b4d572a6d73496039f6db315ddcd80175b8f</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T18:53:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260923-putin-using-citizens-from-47-countries-to-fight-ukraine-zelensky-tells-un--ae57344b771c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260923-putin-using-citizens-from-47-countries-to-fight-ukraine-zelensky-tells-un" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky told the UN General Assembly on Wednesday that Russian President Vladimir Putin had enlisted fighters from 47 countries including North Korea, Ghana and India to fight against Ukraine. Zelensky also warned that his forces could target Russian heating and energy facilities in the winter months if Moscow continues to attack Ukraine's energy infrastructure.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Holy regulation? Pope in Paris to press case for 'disarming' AI</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d3fa6f8798630e31723bc2ff31f0ba9ee4142eeb2329e0be84a325d31e740de7</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T18:44:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260923-holy-regulation-pope-in-paris-to-press-case-for-disarming-ai--69cec545769d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260923-holy-regulation-pope-in-paris-to-press-case-for-disarming-ai" /><summary type="html">It's all about his high holiness here in France. For weeks already, the nation's been abuzz over the upcoming visit of Leo. From Friday evening mass at Notre Dame Cathedral and mass before 600-thousand faithful in Paris to the pilgrimage city of Lourdes and a trip to Metz, hometown of father of European unity Robert Schuman. A papal visit to France usually draws much attention to the symbiotic love-hate relationship between the church and a secular state of mostly-lapsed Catholics. And yes, there have been grumblings about the visit's cost to taxpayers. But the pushback's relatively muted. This new American pope seems genuinely popular here in France. We'll ask why.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>'Breakthrough' archeological find could confirm location of Paris's original settlement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94925ab2e1df177936eaef42aaf8bb2f59fa64b46136596f5732268b0d392938</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T18:19:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260923-breakthrough-archeological-find-could-confirm-paris-origins--3ef95495d245.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260923-breakthrough-archeological-find-could-confirm-paris-origins" /><summary type="html">An ancient wall discovered this summer under a hospital in central Paris is thought to be a fragment of city ramparts built by Iron age settlers. Experts say the stone-and-wood structure could confirm the location of the ancient city of Lutetia.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>🔴Live: 'Russia will never stop,' Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky tells UN</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d53378602a81cb771ef8fa4614f1fcee7e409ccb4f4239f185eb921adc0912f1</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T18:05:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-live-pezeshkian-set-to-address-un-for-the-first-time-since-us-israel-launched-iran-war--40872fea338b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-live-pezeshkian-set-to-address-un-for-the-first-time-since-us-israel-launched-iran-war" /></entry><entry><title>🔴Harvey Weinstein sentenced to 15 years in prison for 2006 sex assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fab3fabeb1603f8e816c033c60746bff18ab44268702e614555c256427eb993b</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:56:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-disgraced-hollywood-mogul-harvey-weinstein-sentenced-to-15-years-for-2006-sex-assault--91ffc4aa930f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-disgraced-hollywood-mogul-harvey-weinstein-sentenced-to-15-years-for-2006-sex-assault" /></entry><entry><title>Disgraced Hollywood mogul Harvey Weinstein sentenced to 15 years for 2006 sex assault</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2215cbfb17d6db4167d56840fc4b3e147de763405785264aa7c5ba68bc9592c3</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:55:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-disgraced-hollywood-mogul-harvey-weinstein-sentenced-to-15-years-for-2006-sex-assault--91ffc4aa930f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-disgraced-hollywood-mogul-harvey-weinstein-sentenced-to-15-years-for-2006-sex-assault" /><summary type="html">Disgraced movie mogul Harvey Weinstein was sentenced to 15 years in prison Wednesday in another #MeToo reckoning for sexually assaulting a former production assistant in 2006.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Iran will 'never bend at the knee', Pezeshkian tells UN in defiant wartime address</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2edf028b250d5e3cddb0b8e8a814ea04a41362510b0a4acbfac1c72496ff7740</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:49:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-iran-will-never-bend-at-the-knee-pezeshkian-tells-un-defiant-wartime-address--10f22d78db02.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260923-iran-will-never-bend-at-the-knee-pezeshkian-tells-un-defiant-wartime-address" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian gave a defiant wartime address at the UN on Wednesday accusing the US of terrorism in his country and saying Iran would not "bend at the knee". But as Pezeshkian called for diplomacy, Iranian officials downplayed their talks with US counterparts on the sidelines of the gerenal assembly as "not anything new".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Backlash against smart glasses grow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc35ce118b1ec7872f1c47bad69a930bcfce5414c7ba408d2a0fc92f95cd7e40</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:30:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/backlash-against-smart-glasses-grow--239c47ee68f4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/backlash-against-smart-glasses-grow" /><summary type="html">Paris prosecutors say they have opened several investigations after receiving complaints about women allegedly filmed on the street without their consent by people wearing so-called “smart glasses”. Calls are growing across Europe for action against what campaigners have dubbed “pervert” smart glasses, after secretly filmed footage of women and girls appeared online. Solange Mougin reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>US says wants Ukraine, Russia to end strikes on energy sites</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:562e0123fe737500e09bbfdcf75dd86ec06f88a5b306dacc194fa65be632abd8</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:25:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-us-says-wants-ukraine-russia-to-end-strikes-on-energy-sites-1--6a47cb7c5c74.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-us-says-wants-ukraine-russia-to-end-strikes-on-energy-sites-1" /><summary type="html">Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy is due to address the UN General Assembly on Wednesday, as US President Donald Trump pushes for an end to Russia’s war and Kyiv seeks to shape renewed diplomatic efforts after more than four and a half years of conflict. France 24 International affairs commentator Douglas Herbert shares further details.</summary></entry><entry><title>Zelenskyy set to address UN as Russia strikes Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e07197c334a6e8cb3d9e674c7be2623f6746069909d3b651e1ae9cda1bc1308f</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:20:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-zelenskyy-set-to-address-un-as-russia-strikes-kyiv-1--602f8dc2d515.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-zelenskyy-set-to-address-un-as-russia-strikes-kyiv-1" /><summary type="html">Russia hammered Ukraine’s capital, Kyiv, with drones in daylight attacks on Wednesday, killing two people and wounding 23, just hours before Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy was due to address world leaders at the UN General Assembly. Zelenskyy met US President Donald Trump on Tuesday, as Trump has expressed frustration over the lack of progress in talks aimed at ending the war and the continued escalation of aerial attacks by both sides. Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iranian president adresses UNGA amid war with US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85ee5728ec376843125d5af1049869ebfc5200154b5ee05aee17956f88d8ce27</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:20:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iranian-president-adresses-unga-amid-war-with-us--55dbecdb0c30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iranian-president-adresses-unga-amid-war-with-us" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian is speaking before the UN General Assembly Wednesday in his first speech at the world body since the US and Israel launched the conflict with his country. His address comes a day after US President Donald Trump told the UNGA he could "annihilate the Islamic Republic" and "drive them into hell".  France 24 correspondent from New York, Jessica Le Masurier, tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why is France's Gen Z turning to Catholicism?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f890671fa317a94c0afb19885bd940d72491057258cf0ccbc331aaf8c02d2a25</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:18:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/france-in-focus/20260923-why-is-france-s-gen-z-turning-to-catholicism--6e00a6b91560.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/france-in-focus/20260923-why-is-france-s-gen-z-turning-to-catholicism" /><summary type="html">As France prepares for Pope Leo XIV's visit, a surprising trend has emerged in recent years: the number of baptisms among teenagers and young adults has skyrocketed. More than 21,000 catechumens, those undergoing the period of preparation for baptism into the Christian Church, have been recorded so far in 2026. How can this renewed interest in the Catholic faith be explained? Florence Gaillard reports for France in Focus.</summary><category term="France in focus" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo XIV to trace back French ancestry, spiritual roots on visit to France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e2333cea50c26e2383838319344a01430efe2b41824dbfa979039f54e983ecdc</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T15:02:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260923-pope-leo-xiv-trace-back-french-ancestry-spiritual-roots-visit-to-france--c0e27df6d9b0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260923-pope-leo-xiv-trace-back-french-ancestry-spiritual-roots-visit-to-france" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo’s four-day visit to France, which kicks off on Friday, is something of a homecoming for the Chicago-born pontiff, a grandson of European immigrants with family roots in Normandy. His spiritual roots in French Catholicism run deeper still.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>El Nino: Climate scientists warn of "Godzilla-level" climate event</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5f3c58d26fdfc5ee2a767ec202390d20675e7675d793ad9dec8887a1c06ca4d1</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:59:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-el-nino-climate-scientists-warn-of-godzilla-level-climate-event--958c99d6c419.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260923-el-nino-climate-scientists-warn-of-godzilla-level-climate-event" /><summary type="html">Extreme heat caused by this year’s “super El Niño” could lead to as many as 451,000 excess deaths worldwide in the six months to February 2027, according to researchers at the University of Chicago’s Climate Impact Lab. The number of extremely hot days is expected to rise by 44%, with Nigeria, Indonesia and Sudan among the countries likely to be worst affected. Researchers warn that the impact could extend well beyond the six-month period studied. Carys Garland reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran’s Pezeshkian tells UN his country is ‘victim’ of US ‘terrorism’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:090d4f8555b68a84bea71bbe1ef51031647e7b844f0ee333154dcde7960beeff</id><updated>2026-09-24T05:03:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T14:57:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-s-pezeshkian-tells-un-his-country-is-victim-of-us-terrorism--68195566b037.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-s-pezeshkian-tells-un-his-country-is-victim-of-us-terrorism" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian has hit back at US President Donald Trump’s speech in his address to the UN General Assembly. He opened by showing images of Iranian civilians killed in US strikes, saying they demonstrated the impact of US and Israeli military action against Iran. During his speech, the US delegation walked out of the General Assembly hall. France 24 International Affairs Editor Kethevane Gorjestani has more.</summary></entry></feed>
